| Step | Location |
|------|----------|
| Local | `e:\Projects\GitRepo\Unisoft.eg\erpnext-develop\erpnext-develop` |
| GitHub | `exdeveloper75/erpnext` → `main` |
| VPS | `root@191.218.163.10`, stack `/opt/frappe_docker`, project `unisoft`, image `exdeveloper75/erpnext:vps1` |
| Public URL | **https://demo.mezanerp.com** (Let's Encrypt via Traefik) |

## HTTPS / Traefik (do not regress)

Production stack uses **HTTPS**, not `compose.noproxy.yaml`.

Compose files (always):

- `compose.yaml`
- `overrides/compose.mariadb.yaml`
- `overrides/compose.redis.yaml`
- `overrides/compose.https.yaml`  ← required (ports 80+443, ACME)
- `overrides/compose.create-site-unisoft.yaml`

`unisoft.env` must keep:

- `SITES_RULE=Host(\`demo.mezanerp.com\`)`
- `LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=admin@mezanerp.com`
- `HTTPS_PUBLISH_PORT=443`
- `FRAPPE_SITE_NAME_HEADER=frontend`
- site `host_name` = `https://demo.mezanerp.com`

**Never** switch back to `compose.noproxy.yaml` for this VPS unless the user asks. After stack recreate, verify `https://demo.mezanerp.com/login` returns 200.

After any `frontend`/`backend` **container recreate**, re-copy Mezan static assets into **both** containers (image layers are separate; `sites/assets` often symlinks to each container’s own `/assets`):

- `erpnext/public/images/mezan-*.svg`
- `erpnext/public/css/unisoft_*.css`, `mezan_dock_top.css`
- `erpnext/public/js/unisoft_*.js`, `mezan_dock_top.js`
- `erpnext/hooks.py` (dock + branding includes)

Then `bench --site frontend clear-cache` and confirm:

- `https://demo.mezanerp.com/assets/erpnext/images/mezan-logo.svg` → 200
- `https://demo.mezanerp.com/assets/erpnext/css/unisoft_login.css` → 200

Long-term: rebuild `exdeveloper75/erpnext:vps1` from GitHub `main` so recreates include these files.

## Installed apps on demo VPS

Required apps on `frontend` site (do not drop):

- `frappe`
- `erpnext` (Mezan fork `exdeveloper75/erpnext`)
- `hrms` (attendance / leave / payroll)
- `payments`

`/opt/frappe_docker/apps.json` must list erpnext + hrms + payments for future image rebuilds. After installing new apps into a running container, `docker commit` into `exdeveloper75/erpnext:vps1` (or rebuild) so recreates keep them.

## Install source rules

- Build/install from **ERPNext GitHub only** (`exdeveloper75/erpnext`).
- Do **not** install from `exdeveloper75/frappe` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do **not** copy images from the old LAN VM (`192.168.217.142`) for VPS deploys.
- Prefer rebuilding/redeploying from GitHub over editing files only inside containers. If a quick container patch is needed for urgency, still sync the same change to local + GitHub afterward.

## Deploy pattern (VPS)

- Image build uses official Frappe `develop` + `apps.json` pointing at `exdeveloper75/erpnext` `main`.
- Compose: `unisoft.env` + `compose.yaml` + mariadb/redis/noproxy + `overrides/compose.create-site-unisoft.yaml`.
- After code changes: rebuild image tag `exdeveloper75/erpnext:vps1` (or migrate/bench update if volumes already have apps), restart stack, clear cache, verify `http://191.218.163.10/login`.

## Mezan top module dock (do not regress)

The workspace module bar must stay **horizontal on top**, not the default left dock.

Protected assets (always keep in repo and on VPS):

- `erpnext/hooks.py` → `app_include_js` must include `/assets/erpnext/js/mezan_dock_top.js`
- `erpnext/hooks.py` → `app_include_css` must include `/assets/erpnext/css/mezan_dock_top.css`
- `erpnext/public/js/mezan_dock_top.js`
- `erpnext/public/css/mezan_dock_top.css`

**Never** restore/checkout `hooks.py` from an older commit, or deploy a partial `hooks.py`, without preserving those two includes. When deploying Construction or other module tarballs that include `hooks.py`, verify `grep mezan_dock hooks.py` on the VPS after extract. After any hooks change: clear-cache + restart backend/frontend.

## Git habits

- Commit when the user asks for the change to be shipped (push is part of this pipeline).
- Never force-push `main` unless explicitly requested.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, passwords, tokens).
